<title>UK: Midland up on Mirror bid.</title>
<headline>Midland up on Mirror bid.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Midland Independent News Plc rose on Friday after British newspaper group Mirror Group Plc said it agreed to buy Midland for 297 million stg, dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares were up 4p at 192-1/2p by 0741 GMT.</p>
<p>Mirror said it was offering 210 pence per share for Midland, which represented a 41 percent premium over Midland's closing price on June 16, the day before the companies announced they were in merger talks.</p>
<p>&quot;It is a recommended bid and it would be very, very unusual for it to not go through,&quot; one analyst said. &quot;It is a sensible price...but the suggestion is that the market may expect a higher bid.&quot;</p>
</text>
